          "signature": "",
          "thinking": "Let me work through this step by step.\n\nLet me define variables:\n- Second field produces: 120 tons\n- First field produces: 2.5 times more than the second\n- Third field produces: 40% less than the first\n\nFirst, I need to be careful about the wording \"2.5 times more than.\" This could mean:\n1. 2.5 times as much as the second (multiplicative interpretation)\n2. 2.5 times more than the second, meaning second + 2.5 × second = 3.5 × second (additive interpretation)\n\nIn common usage, \"2.5 times more\" typically means 2.5 times as much, so I'll interpret it as the first field producing 2.5 times the amount of the second field.\n\nSecond field: 120 tons\n\nFirst field: 2.5 × 120 = 300 tons\n\nThird field: 40% less than the first\nThis means: First field - 40% of first field = 60% of first field\nThird field: 0.6 × 300 = 180 tons\n\nTotal production: 120 + 300 + 180 = 600 tons",
          "type": "thinking"
        },
        {
          "text": "# Total Wheat Production\n\n## Given Information\n- Second field: 120 tons\n- First field: 2.5 times the second field\n- Third field: 40% less than the first field\n\n## Step-by-Step Solution\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the first field's production**\n- First field = 2.5 × Second field\n- First field = 2.5 × 120 = **300 tons**\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the third field's production**\n- Third field = First field − 40% of first field\n- Third field = First field × (100% − 40%) = First field × 60%\n- Third field = 0.6 × 300 = **180 tons**\n\n**Step 3: Calculate total production**\n- Total = First + Second + Third\n- Total = 300 + 120 + 180 = **600 tons**\n\n## Answer\nThe farmer produces **600 tons** of wheat in total.",
